**App name** (30 characters or fewer)
DropLink: Share Files Anywhere

**Short description** (80 characters or fewer)
Share files from your Android phone to any device's browser. No cloud, no cable.

You could also use: "Turn your phone into a private file server for Windows, Mac, Linux and iPhone."

**Full description** (2,842 characters; the limit is 4,000)

DropLink turns your Android phone into a private file server for your own network. Open your music, videos, photos and documents on any other device (Windows PC, Mac, Linux, iPhone, iPad, Chromebook, another Android phone or a smart TV) straight from its web browser. Nothing to install on the other device, no cloud, no account, no cable.

HOW IT WORKS
1. Pick the folders you want to share.
2. Tap Start hosting.
3. On the other device, scan the QR code or open the address shown on your phone.
4. Approve the new device on your phone. That's it.

SHARE WITH ANY DEVICE
• Works with Android, iOS and iPadOS, Windows, macOS, Linux, ChromeOS and more: if it has a modern browser, it can connect.
• Browse your shared folders, preview photos, PDFs and text, and download anything with one tap.
• Only your phone needs the app. Everyone else just uses a browser.

MUSIC AND VIDEO THAT KEEP PLAYING
• A built-in player with queue, shuffle, repeat, speed control and a sleep timer.
• Picks up where you left off, and keeps playing while you browse other folders.
• Lock-screen and notification controls on the connected device.

SEND FILES TO YOUR PHONE
• Connected devices can send files to your phone, but only after you approve: once, or always for a device you trust. You can block a device at any time.
• Received files are saved in Downloads/DropLink.

YOU STAY IN CONTROL
• Folders are shared read-only. DropLink never copies or uploads them.
• Every new device must be approved on your phone, and you can revoke it whenever you like.
• Connections are encrypted with HTTPS and stay on your hotspot or Wi-Fi.
• No ads, no analytics, no trackers, no accounts. Your files never touch our servers, because we don't have any.

BUILT FOR EVERYDAY USE
• Clean, fast web client with light and dark themes and your choice of accent colour.
• Accessibility settings: keyboard shortcuts, screen-reader support, larger text, high contrast and reduced motion.
• Reconnect easily if your phone's address changes.
• Built to keep running in the background, with a warning if Battery Saver might pause it.
• Built-in speed test to check your connection.
• Optional: host a small website or form page from your phone.
• Meet Aubree, the friendly mascot who guides you through each step.

FREE AND OPEN SOURCE
DropLink is free and open source under the Apache 2.0 licence. Read the code, report an issue or suggest an idea on GitHub: github.com/trebronwayne/DropLink

GOOD TO KNOW
• Your phone and the other device must be on the same network, for example your phone's hotspot or the same Wi-Fi.
• Because the connection is encrypted with a certificate made on your phone, a browser may ask you to trust it the first time you connect.
• Keep Battery Saver off while hosting so Android doesn't pause DropLink.

